==============================================================================
V1. The sigma calibration, and its kappa-independence
==============================================================================
  Claim: D_s <= C(B+1)^c L_s 2^{-sigma d_s} => eta = (1-sigma)(alpha*kappa-1),
         and eta < I0(kappa-1/alpha)  <=>  sigma > 1 - I0/alpha = H2(1/alpha).
  Derivation: alpha*kappa-1 = alpha*(kappa-1/alpha), so the condition
     (1-sigma)*alpha*(kappa-1/alpha) < I0*(kappa-1/alpha)
  divides by (kappa-1/alpha) > 0 giving (1-sigma)*alpha < I0, i.e. sigma > 1-I0/alpha.
  => threshold sigma* = 1 - I0/alpha = 0.949955527188
     H2(1/alpha)                    = 0.949955527188   |diff| = 1.11e-16
     assessment claims 0.949955527 -> diff 1.88e-10
  CHECK kappa-independence numerically:
     kappa   alpha*k-1   I0(k-1/a)  sigma* from ratio
      0.65    0.030226    0.001513     0.949955527188
      0.70    0.109474    0.005479     0.949955527188
      0.80    0.267970    0.013410     0.949955527188
      0.90    0.426466    0.021342     0.949955527188
      0.99    0.569113    0.028481     0.949955527188
      1.20    0.901955    0.045138     0.949955527188
      2.00    2.169925    0.108593     0.949955527188
  All equal 1-I0/alpha: the required saving exponent does NOT depend on kappa.
  My earlier report said 'needs exactly 2^-d', i.e. sigma=1.  CORRECTED: sigma>0.949956
  suffices, because the target permits eta>0.  Illustrative (NOT proved):
     kappa=0.9, sigma=0.96: eta=0.017059, exponent=0.945672 IMPROVES (baseline 0.949956)
     kappa=0.99, sigma=0.96: eta=0.022765, exponent=0.944239 IMPROVES (baseline 0.949956)
     kappa=0.65, sigma=0.96: eta=0.001209, exponent=0.949652 IMPROVES (baseline 0.949956)

==============================================================================
V2. The gcd(u,6)=1 qualification
==============================================================================
  m_N(t) = x_w + 2*3^N t, so m_N mod u determines t mod u only if gcd(2*3^N,u)=1.
     u  gcd(u,6)  2*3^N mod u invertible?                        consequence
     3         3                    False m_N mod u is CONSTANT on the cylinder
     5         1                     True             informative test valid
     7         1                     True             informative test valid
     9         3                    False m_N mod u is CONSTANT on the cylinder
    11         1                     True             informative test valid
    15         3                    False m_N mod u is CONSTANT on the cylinder
  So my u=3 and u=9 rows were 0 for a TRIVIAL reason (constant feature), not by CRT.
  The CRT argument is supported only for gcd(u,6)=1; u=5,7,11 are the valid instances.

==============================================================================
V3. The concatenation law for exact realizers
==============================================================================
  Claim: r_{uv} = 3^{-j} (2^a r_v - C_u)  (mod 2^{a+b+1}),  |u|=j, S_u=a, S_v=b.
  Derivation: 3^j m_0 + C_u = 2^a m_j and m_j = r_v (mod 2^{b+1}) give
     3^j m_0 = 2^a m_j - C_u = 2^a r_v - C_u + 2^{a+b+1} t.
  word/split checks over all zero-confined words of length 2..10: 14,405   mismatches: 0
  (the assessment reported 14,405 checks; I get 14,405)

==============================================================================
V4. Full-modulus character factorization within a fixed (j,a) class
==============================================================================
  From V3, e(g r_{uv}/2^{a+b+1}) = e(-g 3^{-j} C_u /2^{a+b+1}) * e(g 3^{-j} 2^a r_v /2^{a+b+1}),
  a product of a PREFIX factor and a SUFFIX factor.  If the admissible (u,v) pairs form a
  product set at fixed (j,a), the full-modulus Weyl sum factors exactly.  Checked:
  product-set (j,a) classes examined: 124 (factorization checked structurally below)
  additive split of the exponent (r_uv = A_v + B_u mod 2^(a+b+1)): 5,756 checks, 0 mismatches
  => the FULL-MODULUS character genuinely factors as (prefix factor)*(suffix factor).
